    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1345" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδιά-φθορος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not affected by decay</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antyll.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				46.22.3
			</span></i>; <i>uncorrupted, chaste</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				252d
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">απ᾽ ὀρθῆς. . καὶ ἀδιαφθόρου τῆς ψυχῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.298
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				984
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				1.59
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.5e
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ρως, ἐρᾶσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					1.137
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of judges,
				<i>incorruptible</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				768b
			</span></i>; of witnesses, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1376a17
			</span></i>; of magistrates, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1286a39
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				2.240b13
			</span></i>. 
				Sup.
			
			Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτατα</span> Pl.l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>imperishable</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				106e
			</span></i>.</div>
